dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hey, carolyn. how are you?
[patient] hi, good to see you. i'm doing okay.
[doctor] good to see you too. so, how are you doing with your elbows?
[patient] they've been flaring up a little lately.
[doctor] okay. so, your osteoarthritis has been flaring up a little lately. and, um, you know, i know you're working a lot in the office. so, do you feel like you're sitting at the computer all day?
[patient] yeah, i do. i don't know if it's just because i'm sitting in the same position all day.
[doctor] okay. so, does one elbow bother you more than the other?
[patient] my right elbow bothers me more than my left elbow, but i'm typing all day versus writing.
[doctor] okay. any other joint pain?
[patient] no, no other joint pain.
[doctor] okay. and then you've had some numbness and tingling in your hands. do you still have that?
[patient] yeah, occasionally. i try to shake out my arms to relieve the numbness.
[doctor] okay. and, um, you know, i know that you have a history of gout. how are you doing with that?
[patient] it's been okay. my last episode was about three months ago. i had some inflammation in my toe at that time.
[doctor] okay. and, um, have you had any other issues with that?
[patient] no, i haven't.
[doctor] okay. and you're still on the colchicine 0.6 milligrams twice a day as needed for the flare-ups of your gout?
[patient] yes, that's correct.
[doctor] okay. and how are you doing with your psoriasis?
[patient] it's under control. it's not a major problem for me.
[doctor] okay. so, i'm gon na go ahead and do a quick physical exam, okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] hey, dragon, show me the vital signs. so, your vital signs look good. your blood pressure is 120 over 80, heart rate is 72, respiratory rate is 16, and your temperature is 98.6. so, let's go ahead and do a quick physical exam. so, your neck is supple without lymphadenopathy. your lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally. no wheezes, rales, or rhonchi. your heart is regular rate and rhythm. your abdomen is soft. no masses or tenderness to palpation. no hepatosplenomegaly. and on your musculoskeletal exam, no edema to your lower extremities. so, let me look at your right elbow. there is some edema and inflammation of the right olecranon. some tenderness to palpation of the olecranon bursa. pain with pronation and supination. pain with flexion and extension of the right arm. so, carolyn, i'm gon na go ahead and order an x-ray of your right elbow. i'm gon na order a right elbow x-ray. and we'll see what's going on in there. how does that sound?
[patient] that sounds good.
[doctor] okay. and, um, for your osteoarthritis, i'm gon na go ahead and prescribe meloxicam 15 milligrams once a day for the pain and swelling. okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and for your gout, we'll continue the colchicine 0.6 milligrams twice a day as needed for flare-ups. and for your psoriasis, continue the steroid cream. okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. do you have any questions?
[patient] no, that's fine.
[doctor] okay. hey, dragon, go ahead and order the x-ray. and, um, i'll have my nurse come in and get you discharged. okay?
[patient] okay, sounds good. thank you.
[doctor] thank you. }}<|eot_id|>
