dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi beverly it's good to see you today so i see that you're here for your annual exam how have you been doing
[patient] i've been doing well i started working at a bakery this summer so that's been fun
[doctor] yeah that sounds fun i'm sure it's a lot of fun working at a bakery so how's your diabetes been
[patient] it's been a little up and down my blood sugars have been fluctuating a lot i think because of my diet but i'm trying to eat better
[doctor] okay and how have you been doing with your metformin are you taking it as prescribed
[patient] yes i am i haven't missed any doses
[doctor] okay and your blood pressure has been okay
[patient] yeah my blood pressure has been good
[doctor] okay and are you taking your lisinopril
[patient] yes i am
[doctor] okay good how about your diet have you been able to keep that under control
[patient] i've been trying to eat better i have been eating more sweets because of work but i'm trying to cut that out
[doctor] okay that makes sense that that can be tough especially when you're working at a bakery but it's good that you're trying to make some changes so how have you been sleeping
[patient] i've been sleeping well i get a full eight hours
[doctor] okay and have you had any thoughts of self-harm or suicidal ideations
[patient] no i have not
[doctor] okay that's good to hear so i'm gon na go ahead and do a quick physical exam on you i'll start with your neurological exam your grip strength is equal bilaterally and your neurologically intact i'm gon na check your neck your neck is supple without thyromegaly or lymphadenopathy no carotid bruits appreciable i'm gon na listen to your lungs your lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally no wheezes rales or rhonchi i'm gon na check your heart your heart has a regular rate and rhythm grade two over six systolic ejection murmur no gallops or rubs no extra heart sounds good pulses and i'm gon na check your abdomen your abdomen is soft to palpation no hepatosplenomegaly or masses i'm gon na check your feet i'm gon na look at the back of your feet and i do see some calluses on the bottom of your feet but no ulcers or sores so i'm gon na go ahead and review your results your hemoglobin a1c is elevated so let's go ahead and talk a little bit about my assessment and plan for you so for your diabetes you have had some issues with keeping your blood sugars under control i know you said you've been trying to make some dietary changes but it sounds like you're still having some issues with that so i want you to continue taking your metformin twice a day i want you to check your fasting blood glucose levels each morning and call them in to me about two weeks from now we will follow up in about two months and at that time we can discuss further treatment recommendations for you your blood pressure looks like it's been relatively stable so i'm going to continue you on your lisinopril ten milligrams once daily and i want you to continue to monitor that and let me know if you have any issues with that do you have any questions for me
[patient] no that sounds good
[doctor] okay great so i'll have the nurse come in and get you discharged and we'll see you back in two months
[patient] okay sounds good thank you
[doctor] you're welcome }}<|eot_id|>
