dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi susan, how are you today?
[patient] i'm doing well, doctor, just here for a high blood pressure check.
[doctor] okay, so you're here for a high blood pressure check. how have you been feeling?
[patient] i've been feeling alright. i've just noticed that my blood pressure has been a little high, especially recently.
[doctor] okay, and what have you been doing to check your blood pressure at home?
[patient] i've been checking it with a monitor at home. it's been running around 150 over 90.
[doctor] okay, that's a bit high. are you taking any medication for your high blood pressure?
[patient] yes, i'm taking norvasc 10 milligrams daily.
[doctor] okay, and have you had any side effects from the norvasc?
[patient] no, i've not noticed any side effects.
[doctor] okay, and have you had any other symptoms like chest pain or shortness of breath?
[patient] no chest pain or shortness of breath.
[doctor] any headaches?
[patient] yes, i've had some headaches, but i'm not sure if it's from stress at work or the high blood pressure.
[doctor] okay, well, we'll check that out. how about your kidney transplant? how's that going?
[patient] it's going well. i'm taking all of my immunosuppressive medications.
[doctor] okay, good to hear. i'm gon na go ahead and do a quick physical exam on you. i'm gon na call out some of my findings as i go along. so, you're in no apparent distress. your neck is supple, no thyromegaly or lymphadenopathy. your lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally, no wheezes, rales or rhonchi. your heart has a two over six systolic ejection murmur, but that's been present on previous exams. you have no edema. your scar on your left flank from the kidney transplant is healed and looks good. i'm gon na go ahead and check your vitals. your blood pressure is 160 over 98. your heart rate is 76. your respiratory rate is 16. your temperature is 98.6, and your oxygen saturation is 98 % on room air. so, i'm gon na go ahead and order a lipid panel and a metabolic panel to check your kidney function. i also reviewed your ecg that was done before you came in, and everything looks normal. so, for your high blood pressure, i'd like to add carvedilol 25 milligrams twice a day. this will help bring your blood pressure down. i also recommend some diet changes, such as reducing your salt intake and increasing your intake of fruits and vegetables. do you have any questions about that?
[patient] no, that sounds good.
[doctor] okay, great. for your kidney transplant, continue with your current medications. i'll also go ahead and order a repeat kidney function panel. any other questions for me?
[patient] no, that's it.
[doctor] okay, great. i'll see you back in a month to check your blood pressure. if you have any questions or concerns before then, feel free to call the office.
[patient] okay, thank you, doctor.
[doctor] you're welcome. }}<|eot_id|>
