[doctor] okay so on physical exam you appear to be in no distress you don't have a fever you don't have any tobacco or other substance use you're alert and oriented you don't appear anxious agitated or depressed your jvp is flat with your head at ninety degrees your respiratory exam is clear you don't have any cough or shortness of breath your lungs are clear to percussion and auscultation and your breathing is unlabored you have no cva tenderness your heart rhythm is regular you don't have any murmur or gallop you don't have any ankle edema and your skin is moist and you have good capillary refill so everything looks good on your physical exam so let's go ahead and talk a little bit about my assessment and my plan so for your alcohol use disorder i'm gon na start you on the naltrexone and we'll do the injectable form and we'll start you on may seventeenth and we'll do the second injection on june fourteenth and we'll follow up with you and see how you're doing with that and we'll see if we can cut back on the alcohol and i think that that will be really beneficial for your blood pressure and for your overall health and for your hypercholesterolemia i'm gon na order the influenza vaccination and the shingrix vaccination number two i know that you deferred that last time and i think that that's something that we should get you up to date on and we'll continue you on the lisinopril ten milligrams a day and the hydrochlorothiazide twelve point five milligrams once a day and i think that your blood pressure will improve significantly if you can cut back on the alcohol and we'll see you back in the office the week of june fourteenth for your second injection and we'll follow up with you and see how you're doing with that and we'll see if we can get your blood pressure down to one thirty to one forty over seventy to eighty okay
