dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, ms. ross. how are you?
[patient] i'm doing alright.
[doctor] so, what brings you in today?
[patient] i'm here for a full-spectrum std test.
[doctor] okay. and i see here that you're experiencing some symptoms. can you tell me a little bit more about those?
[patient] yeah. i've been having some discomfort and a change in discharge and odor in my vaginal area. the right side of my vagina is starting to become painful.
[doctor] mm-hmm. and when did you start noticing these symptoms?
[patient] i started noticing the change in the odor, color and consistency of my discharge last week. the pain started a few days ago and it has not gone away.
[doctor] okay. any fever or chills?
[patient] no, no fever or chills.
[doctor] okay. and i see here that you recently learned that your partner of three years has been engaging in sexual encounters with other people. is that correct?
[patient] yeah. i found out recently.
[doctor] okay. and you want to be evaluated for all sexually transmitted diseases?
[patient] yes, i do.
[doctor] okay. have you had any abnormal pap smears in the past?
[patient] i had an abnormal pap smear around the age of 20, but all my pap smears since then, including the one about six months ago, were normal.
[doctor] okay. thank you. let's go ahead and do a physical exam. i'm just gon na take a look at you. i'm gon na be as gentle as i can. okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] alright. your external genitalia look normal. no external lesions. normal labia majora and labia minora. normal physiological discharge with normal color and odor. i'm gon na check your cervix. okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] your cervix looks normal. your vaginal wall is normal. no cervical motion tenderness or masses noted. i'm gon na go ahead and swab for the std testing. we'll be checking for gonorrhea, chlamydia, trichomoniasis, syphilis, hiv, and hepatitis c. i'll call you with the results of the laboratory testing. do you have any questions?
[patient] no, that's it.
[doctor] okay. thank you. }}<|eot_id|>
