[patient] yeah, but it hurts.
[doctor] okay. you do have pain with abduction and adduction to about 90 degrees only. does it hurt when i rotate your arm like this?
[patient] yes, that hurts.
[doctor] okay. i can appreciate your radial artery pulse. let's look at your x-ray. okay, so your x-ray shows an acute fracture of the acromioclavicular joint. i'm going to order a ct of your right shoulder to further evaluate that. i'm gon na go ahead and order a ct of your right shoulder to further evaluate that. i'm going to place you in a sling and prescribe meloxicam 15 milligrams once a day for the pain. i'm also going to recommend formal physical therapy to strengthen your right shoulder in hopes of avoiding surgery in the future. in the meantime, i do recommend that you avoid tackle football.
