dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hey alexis how are you today
[patient] i'm doing okay thanks how about you
[doctor] i'm doing well thanks for asking so i see here in the notes that you've been having some right hand pain can you tell me a little bit about what's been going on
[patient] yeah so it's been about six months now where i've been having these like intermittent episodes of numbness and tingling in my fingers and it's just been getting worse over the past month or so
[doctor] okay and which fingers are you noticing this numbness and tingling in
[patient] it's like my thumb index and middle fingers
[doctor] okay and has it become constant over the past month or so
[patient] yeah it's pretty much constant now
[doctor] okay and is there any pain associated with it
[patient] yeah it's painful when i'm typing and using a mouse and i use those a lot because i'm on a keyboard all day
[doctor] okay and have you noticed any sleep disturbances at all
[patient] no no sleep disturbances
[doctor] okay and have you tried anything for relief
[patient] yeah i've tried rest and ibuprofen and those have been the most helpful
[doctor] okay so just to confirm you're taking ibuprofen for the pain
[patient] yeah that's right
[doctor] okay and have you been taking it regularly
[patient] yeah i take it a few times a day when it starts to hurt
[doctor] okay and how much are you taking
[patient] i take 200 milligrams four times a day
[doctor] okay and it seems to help
[patient] yeah it helps a little bit
[doctor] okay and what do you do for work
[patient] i work on a keyboard all day
[doctor] okay and you mentioned that you do a lot of typing and using a mouse
[patient] yeah i do
[doctor] okay and so that's been going on for six months and it's just been getting progressively worse over the past month
[patient] yeah that's correct
[doctor] okay and have you tried any other treatments or medications
[patient] no i've just been sticking with the ibuprofen and resting
[doctor] okay and does the pain or the numbness wake you up at night
[patient] no it doesn't wake me up at night
[doctor] okay and so you've been experiencing pain in the first second and third digits on your right hand and you're having numbness and tingling in those same digits as well
[patient] yeah that's right
[doctor] okay let's go ahead and take a look at your hand alright so i'm going to check the strength in your hand can you squeeze my fingers
[patient] okay
[doctor] okay can you squeeze a little bit harder
[patient] okay
[doctor] okay now i'm noticing that your grip strength on your right hand is decreased compared to your left hand and when i move your wrist like this does that cause any pain
[patient] yeah that hurts
[doctor] okay and when i tap on the inside of your wrist here does that cause any tingling or pain
[patient] yeah that's tingling
[doctor] okay that's a positive tinsel's sign alright so i'm gon na order an emg nerve conduction study of your right hand and wrist to further evaluate your symptoms and i'm gon na go ahead and order an x-ray of your right hand and wrist as well to rule out any bony abnormalities now based on your symptoms and your exam it sounds like you have carpal tunnel syndrome so let's talk a little bit about what that is and what we can do to treat it carpal tunnel syndrome is a condition where the median nerve that runs through your wrist is compressed at the wrist and can cause pain numbness and tingling in the thumb and the first three fingers of the hand and this is often caused by repetitive movements such as typing or using a mouse and it can be quite painful and it can interfere with your daily activities so for treatment of this i would like you to continue taking the ibuprofen but i would like to increase the dose to six hundred milligrams four times a day and i'm also gon na recommend that you wear a wrist splint at night and this will help to alleviate some of the symptoms and i'm gon na also order that emg nerve conduction study to further evaluate your symptoms and if the study is positive we can consider additional treatment with physical therapy or even surgical intervention with a carpal tunnel release so do you have any questions about that
[patient] no that sounds good
[doctor] okay alright so we will get that ordered for you and i'll see you back in about four weeks to check on your progress
[patient] okay sounds good thank you
[doctor] you're welcome }}<|eot_id|>
